    {
      "area": "control and treatment",
      "result": "pass",
      "evidence": "The reference plan reconstructs exactly the immutable R26 candidate overlay on original labels. The treatment selects accepted R28 train labels only for eligible photos. Held015 and31 excluded old-series photos retain identical R26 bytes. The actual input delta is10 coordinate-replaced rows in9 photos, with no added/deleted rows or class/visibility changes."
    },
    {
      "area": "evaluation isolation",
      "result": "pass",
      "evidence": "Every val plan uses original source bytes in both arms:20 photos/664 objects. R28 development labels do not enter trainer supervision. Frozen666/663 reference manifests and counts are independently hash-verified; R28 review is explicitly exploratory."
    },
    {
      "area": "initialization and numerical recipe",
      "result": "pass",
      "evidence": "Both full arms select the same seed46 recipe hash, 30epochs, batch4, imgsz1280, FP32, AdamW lr0=0.0001, original epoch173 initializer, and final last.pt checkpoint. The resource trial uses the candidate and cannot initialize full runs. Initializer bytes were verified by executed preflight."
    },
    {
      "area": "paired runtime and recovery",
      "result": "pass_by_source_inspection",
      "evidence": "The preserved notebook requires equal recorded runtime for the pair and matching available runtime before a missing arm starts. Completed artifacts are verified before reuse; different source/protocol pins or incomplete runs are not silently reused."
    },
    {
      "area": "staging and return provenance",
      "result": "pass_by_source_inspection_and_input_execution",
      "evidence": "Staging independently hashes image/label bytes. The new source record carries the entire training-input delta and its bound digest; checkpoint validation recomputes it. Reference training-label identity is explicitly r26_predecessor_control. Packaging verifies both staging source records and the embedded report/hash before returning the existing paired bundle format."
    },
    {
      "area": "source-pinned notebook builder",
      "result": "pass_by_source_inspection",
      "evidence": "CLI generation requires a full source commit and compares all442 collected source paths with git show, including157 complete R28 review labels,92 candidate overlay labels, effective predecessor labels, and recursively referenced new evidence/policy files. A Git LFS pointer must match materialized payload SHA256 and size. The generated code cell pins source commit, protocol path/hash and experiment id. Draft generation remains internal and explicitly reported; final CLI uses strict verification."
    }
  ],
